I loved the game and would totally rate it 9.0/10; no sweat!
The game falls into the catergory of survival horror and, therefore, you have no guns to work with (which is nice).
Pros:
- The game is really immersive and can frighten the♥♥♥♥♥♥outta you;
- Clean HUD;
- No MAP/minimap or objective tracker, things that would basically kill the exploration/survival part of the game. The game isn't open world so you'll hardly ever get lost in it (some might find this a CON, which I strongly disagree);
- The story is great and compelling;
- There are several puzzles that you must solve to advance in the game;
- You'll get 10~12h of gameplay (it depends on how you play it);
- It's worth the money invested (got it for sub $7 on a sale).
Cons:
- For some, the graphics might feel outdated (it didn't bother me at all);
- (MY SOLE DISAPPOINTMENT) The visual effect that the devs chose to show that you're hurt is HORRIBLE, it's a horrific color distortion that you have on screen. It feels like you have a faulty GPU/Monitor/video cable and it totally HURTS the eyes. It's impossible to be looking at the screen for longer than two minutes w/o feeling your eyes "burning".

